4. elb-pr/claudikins-kernel — MIT (structural influence, no copied text)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `brain-jam-plan` skill from the Claudikins kernel
(https://github.com/elb-pr/claudikins-kernel/blob/main/skills/brain-jam-plan/SKILL.md)
informed the planning-discipline sections added to `intent-ops` in v3.1.0. No text was
copied: every sentence in the affected sections was written for this repository. What was
adopted is structural and methodological, listed here for transparency rather than because
the MIT License compels it for idea-level reuse:

    - the "Rationalizations to Resist" / "Red Flags — STOP and Reassess" section pairing,
      and its two-column excuse/reality table format
    - Effort and Risk columns on the approach-comparison table, with an explicit
      "recommend one, the user decides" rule
    - "never fabricate research" as a non-negotiable, which seeded the Evidence Discipline
      sections

Affected files:

    intent-ops/skills/plan-writer/SKILL.md          (Phase 3.5, Rationalizations, Red Flags)
    intent-ops/skills/spec-writer/SKILL.md          (Phase 3, Rationalizations, Red Flags)
    intent-ops/skills/plan-executor/SKILL.md        (Rationalizations)

Note that two of these conventions predate this influence in `intent-ops`: the
"Common Rationalizations" table has been in `tdd-guide` since v2.0.0 by way of
obra/superpowers (section 1), which is where the pattern originates, and `spec-writer`
already presented 2–3 approaches before v1.1.0.

